# __PROJECT__

An agent built on [Psych](https://github.com/psych-systems/psych-runtime).

```sh
python main.py
```

It runs with no API key: without one it uses Psych's scriptable fake model, so
the whole agent loop executes offline. To call a real provider:

```sh
export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
export PSYCH_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini          # optional
export PSYCH_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1   # optional: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
python main.py
```

## What to change first

- **Add a tool.** Write a function with type hints and a docstring, pass it in
  `tools=[...]`, and name it in the Spec's `tools=(psych_runtime.CodeTool(name=...),)`.
- **Change the instructions.** That is the system prompt.
- **Keep the Runs.** `psych_runtime.session()` defaults to an in-memory store, which
  loses everything when the process exits. Pass `store=PostgresStore(dsn=...)`
  once you want them to survive.

## Where to look next

`psych doctor` reports what is installed and configured.

If you use an AI coding agent, `psych skills install` drops 26 guides into
`.agents/skills/`, one per feature, so it can write correct Psych code without
guessing.
